ENTRY            33218   20260715   20261124   20261124       3224
SUBENT        33218001   20260715   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                  8         21
TITLE      Intriguing features of the prompt fission gamma-ray
            spectra in the fast neutron induced fission of 232Th
AUTHOR     (S.De, R.G.Thomas, G.Mishra, G.Mohanto, A.Kumar)
INSTITUTE  (3INDTRM)
           (3INDIND) Homi Bhabha National Institute, Mumbai
REFERENCE  (J,EPJ/A,61,38,2025)
           #doi:10.1140/epja/s10050-025-01508-6
DETECTOR   (IOCH) A parallel-plate ionization chamber with two
            independent sections, operating in air, was used as
            the fission detector. Each section consisted of
            copper-plated 1.5 mm thick G-10 discs of diameter
            7.5 cm, separated by 2.0 mm thick Teflon spacers.
           (SCIN) Two 38.1 mm x 38.1 mm cylindrical CeBr3
            detectors were placed in the target plane at distances
            of 21.0 cm and 22.5 cm from the target center. The
            threshold of the detectors were set at 100 keV
METHOD     (COINC)
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) Uncertainty due to statistical and unfolding
            were considered.
HISTORY    (20260828R) Data received from R.G. Thomas
           (20260715C) G.Mohanto, Mareena Thomas
ENDBIB              21
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           24
